 "operation": [
  {
   "topic": "Wire clamping",
   "page": 2,
   "text": "Each position is a screw connection with tension sleeve, driven by a slotted screw. Strip length is 7 mm and tightening torque 0.5 to 0.6 Nm. One clamp takes two wires of equal cross-section within the two-conductor limits."
  },
  {
   "topic": "Holding the block while tightening",
   "page": 3,
   "text": "A defined tightening torque applies to every connection. Two- and three-position blocks are supported while a wire is fastened, held by hand or braced against the housing, as the single solder pin at a clamp does not take up that torque."
  },
  {
   "topic": "Lining up",
   "page": 1,
   "text": "The housings latch together at the sides, so blocks of the family combine into any number of positions on the same 5.08 mm grid."
  },
  {
   "topic": "Temperature",
   "page": 5,
   "text": "Operating ambient is -40 to 105 °C, limited by the current-carrying capacity (derating) curve. Ambient plus the block's own temperature rise stays at or under its upper limit temperature. Assembly: -5 to 100 °C. Storage and transport: -40 to 70 °C at 30 to 70 % relative humidity."
  },
  {
   "topic": "PCB layout",
   "page": 7,
   "text": "Drill 1.3 mm holes on a 5.08 mm pitch. The hole row is 4.6 mm behind the wire-entry face, and the first hole is 2.54 mm in from the end face, so a block of n positions spans n × 5.08 mm."
  }
 ],
